{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/876-advice-for-cheiron-group-as-antagonists","id":876,"title":"Advice for Cheiron Group as antagonists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-01T20:53:12-07:00","id":876,"title":"Advice for Cheiron Group as antagonists","content":"So I'll clarify that I'm a Mage guy primarily, but Cheiron Group clicks for me from the descriptions I've read. I'm willing to fork over the money for whatever books I might need in order to run them as antagonists, not just for Mage but for other games as well.<br /> <br /> To that extent, do you guys have any advice for how to characterize them or use them? Do you have any stories of using them you want to share? They're definitely seeming like they'd make great antagonists and protagonists!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-02T21:12:30-07:00","id":1498,"title":"","content":"Cheiron is my favorite Hunter group. I'll see if I can help. The most obvious way to use them is to send a field team to try and capture the Player Characters. The horror should set in when they realize that they're being shot at with tranquilizer darts, that they're going to be captured instead of killed. Cheiron employees are well-trained, with the good cells being more akin to bounty hunters and professional mercenaries instead of any corporate paper-pusher. Have them chatter about &quot;carving you up for scrap&quot; and how much their parts will be worth. Really fixate on how gnarly their Thaumatechnology implants are; these guys are stitched-together with bits and pieces of things like you. The big theme here is human inhumanity: they see other living things as product, nothing else, and are willing to become monsters in the pursuit of that. Alternatively, you can use them like how Pentex was back in the oWoD. Cheiron has its fingers in damn near everything; their products are all but universal. Maybe a product goes out that has horrific side effects, clearly tainted by something supernatural. The paper trail leads back to a Cheiron lab, where they have vampires in small cages being bled repeatedly, or a werewolf who is alive but vivisected, his organs harvested each time they grow back. You're aiming for the kind of horror PETA likes in their videos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T07:40:29-08:00","id":1753,"title":"","content":"I'm preferring to keep them as being specialized monster hunter/acquirer types.<br /> <br /> Do they have any sort of outfit that they use regularly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T08:27:14-08:00","id":1795,"title":"","content":"Depending on how much of a hard time you want to give your players, you could play up Cheiron's corporate power. It's not just the cell of hunters with guns, tactics and Thaumatech that they need to fear; it's all the resources the corporation can throw after them if the executives decide it's worth the expense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T08:43:17-08:00","id":1811,"title":"","content":"The core states that they only are issued a jacket with a stylized Cheiron logo on it that's barely recognizable to the official corporate logo. Other than that, it can run the gamut from paramilitary gear and equipment to a bunch of guys in normal clothes with tentacles shooting out of their legs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T14:48:58-08:00","id":2922,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that they also subvert and infiltrate, compacts and conspiracies reveals that they employ spies among the vampires and witches, even giving them thaumatech in return for their services.<br /> <br /> Is this a mage game you're intending? Then have a mage enemy/rival be one of those cheiron agents, sending the hit squads after them, using their magic to enable cheiron to harass and threaten the players.<br /> <br /> For something a bit more world turning, do you remember that storyline based on Children of Men in which a child is Awake before it was even born? One of the proposed possibilities in that scenario is that a biological agent for awakening be reverse engineered from that kid. What if Cheiron discovered awakening in an injection? Another option was that the mage baby was fathered by an outsider revenant, making the kid more anti-christ than messiah. Perhaps that's what cheiron reverse engineered, maybe they're making mages who channel not the power of the supernal realms but the abyss itself or a lower realm.<br /> <br /> If you're open to using psychics from the mage chronicler's guide, perhaps cheiron is manufacturing them, or successfully discovered how to harvest their brain tissue for psychic power.<br /> <br /> If you're thinking another gameline let me know and I'll see what comes to mind, but I'm not feeling inclined to sprout ideas for a gameline you're not interested in, lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 11-04-2013, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T05:57:25-08:00","id":3405,"title":"","content":"When I run Cherion as antagonists its with a few corporate suits sending off scores of goons into battle to get whoever or whatever it is they want to harvest. Are the people they send up to the challenge? Mostly not, but then it's a numbers game. If they send enough men in armor and guns after someone even as resourceful as a mage, the mage has to win every engagement and Cherion only has to get lucky once. Also, in the corporate environment of today I like to think Cherion subcontracts some of their retrievals to private security firms. Gives you an excuse to blow the dust off that copy of Dogs of War!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/759-willr","name":"WillR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T06:18:55-08:00","id":3426,"title":"","content":"Cheiron has resources. That defines them.<br /> <br /> They can afford to send as many teams as they need after you, because they'll always have more waiting in the wings. The cannon fodder will be exactly that, but once they get serious, they'll be sending the best people money can buy. Security contractors? Oh yeah. Illegal hitmen? You know it. And this is before they start busting out the corporate ghouls, the number of slashers they employ, and all the folks loaded up with Thaumatech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T17:29:30-08:00","id":23401,"title":"","content":"Another way you can play up their power is, after Cheiron has made a few runs at the characters, have one of their cars explode before they get in it (or after, if they can take it): great way to play up the paranoia of the players, soon they'll be checking their car <i>very</i> carefully before they get in it every time, scanning the pizza they ordered for poison, checking every product they buy against a list of products created by Cheiron or their subsidiaries (obviously, make the list extremely extensive); this one is particularly effective if you give one of the characters a very minor penalty to their magic, with the justification (not that they know) that Cheiron slips a drug into their peanuts/butter/soft drink that inhibits magic.<br /> <br /> Plus, they're a corporation, which means they can make the characters lives difficult in a thousand little ways: slip some money to the tax department, characters get audited. Call in a report of a crime, characters have to deal with police (and if they end up in gaol, then that makes it that much easier to swipe them). Buy the lands around the characters houses, set up agents in there to watch the characters. If the characters get their cars serviced or fixed, maybe an agent bribes the mechanic to let him place a tracking bug in the car where it can't be seen.<br /> <br /> And that's all before we start considering supernatural options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T06:33:16-08:00","id":23716,"title":"","content":"My suggestion; play them as normal family men who happen to be quite happy to lock you up, experiment on you, eventually kill you, and if you asked them why they wouldn't be able to give you an answer that they found satisfying.<br /> <br /> Cheiron isn't the people. It's not the executive deciding that an extra million in profits is worth the life of a little changeling girl. It's not the doctor who's willing to put aside his ethics for the paycheck or the cure for cancer. It' not even the hunters who bring in the monsters.<br /> <br /> Cheiron is the system that turns ordinary people into the monstrosity we know and love from Hunter. It's the way an executive can set a target and promise any extra profits can go into whatever project the doctor wants without seeing that turn into a cut corner, near a Changeling girl's heart. It's the distance between a hunter persuading a Mage to come in for some simple brain scans and the laboratory that lets that hunter pretend he doesn't know what's going to happen.<br /> <br /> <br /> Focus on the system and how no snowflake ever believes itself to be responsible for the avalanche. Good people who manage to ignore what they're doing because they have their eye on the prize, be it money or medicine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T13:17:45-08:00","id":23926,"title":"","content":"In the game I'm running right now, they developed Pigment (from Orpheus) and let it leak to a drug dealer to test it's ultimate effects on humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/906-qoorl","name":"Qoorl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T10:25:37-08:00","id":25222,"title":"","content":"Cheiron is the WoD's version of the Umbrella Corporation. They have field agents, researchers, thaumatech, but especially ressources: They can easily purchase a private army to hunt you down. They're ingenious in utilizing everything they can. The group leaving an Artifact or Imbued Item behind? Bad decision. Someone finds it, sells it, Cheiron gets their fingers on it. Then they theorize about massproducing it, coming to the point where they want those Mages for themselves to &quot;question&quot; them. Maybe they trick them, buy them, or buy one of their allies off to betray them to Cheiron.<br /> The primary aspect of Cheiron is its size: Nearly no one knows which person of company belongs to the group. In a world where money is power, Cheiron is king.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/239565-wizard-s-panoply-how-to-play-a-mage-in-exalted-collection-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Complete the Wizard's Panoply</a></b> [How to be a mage in Creation]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/442-nephtys","name":"Nephtys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar442_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T19:15:23-08:00","id":25512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nephtys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/876-advice-for-cheiron-group-as-antagonists?p=25222#post25222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cheiron is the WoD's version of the Umbrella Corporation. They have field agents, researchers, thaumatech, but especially ressources: They can easily purchase a private army to hunt you down. They're ingenious in utilizing everything they can. The group leaving an Artifact or Imbued Item behind? Bad decision. Someone finds it, sells it, Cheiron gets their fingers on it. Then they theorize about massproducing it, coming to the point where they want those Mages for themselves to &quot;question&quot; them. Maybe they trick them, buy them, or buy one of their allies off to betray them to Cheiron.<br /> The primary aspect of Cheiron is its size: Nearly no one knows which person of company belongs to the group. In a world where money is power, Cheiron is king.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely Ditched the Cheiron name in my games and blatantly called them Umbrella.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T19:39:52-08:00","id":25522,"title":"","content":"Related question: So I kind of want to yank the Orochi Group from The Secret World, at least for the namesake, but I feel weird having two Group groups. Does anyone have any suggestions for alternate things to call The Cheiron Group? I'm considering only referring to the corporation as Cheiron, and calling the people by Field Projects Division. But I wouldn't mind a nice whole name for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T22:52:50-08:00","id":25615,"title":"","content":"You could call them The Cerberus Foundation, in an homage to Dante's Inferno and it's use of Cheiron as the guardian of Hell's circle of violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/213-darkhunter","name":"Darkhunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T23:09:10-08:00","id":80828,"title":"","content":"Bringing this back. My girlfriend is set to start running Vampire for our group soon and I'm excited by the idea. We've been throwing around plot ideas and I've been introducing her to different stuff, and she's expressed interest in using Cheiron in Vampire.<br /> <br /> Any suggestions/thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T17:19:09-08:00","id":81328,"title":"","content":"Watch all the Buffy episodes that feature the &quot;Initiative&quot; in the season she goes to college. The Cheiron Group is basically the Initiative with corporate backers instead of military contracts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T23:01:47-08:00","id":81435,"title":"","content":"Also, what would the Corporate logo be like versus the FPD logo?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T12:06:31-08:00","id":81713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/876-advice-for-cheiron-group-as-antagonists?p=81435#post81435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, what would the Corporate logo be like versus the FPD logo?</div> </div> </div> </div> Corporate is the symbol accused of being Satanic. FPD is that bow and arrow we see in the art. I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T12:25:58-08:00","id":81728,"title":"","content":"That's correct. The corporate logo is a reference to <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Procter_%26_Gamble#Logo_controversy\" target=\"_blank\">this one</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}